# Scoped to backtest-artifacts/ only.
#
# Same reasoning as backtest-data/publish/.gitattributes: this repository's
# default Windows checkout has core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF
# for anything Git treats as text. Every file under this tree - the sealed
# preregistration, the roster/cohort/initial-lineup artifacts, and the
# freeze-sequence outputs (Commit M's MDE artifact, Commit B's manifest) -
# is canonically serialized with a bare LF and is byte-hashed/git-blob-
# compared elsewhere (freezeHash, CI's byte-compare of a regenerated
# artifact against the committed one). An autocrlf rewrite on a Windows
# checkout would silently change those bytes without changing what the file
# means, which is exactly the class of drift the freeze exists to rule out.

* text eol=lf
